{"seconds": 24.915130875073373, "submission_file": "experiments/generation-repairs-v1/submissions/C05/gpt-5.6-sol/format-r1.json", "submission_sha256": "6691eddacfa33b624b186a7abf645f653d644d0f0c9fde9367ccdcff47fe891b", "code_sha256": "4008691381e7a2cbac9b80bcfa5964655b08fd79d2a02d960d65c7547250909f", "description": "Bins calcium and spikes into the exact 40-ms evaluation grid, normalizes each neuron robustly, and extracts acausal multiscale level, slope, curvature, and candidate-deconvolution features. A Poisson histogram gradient booster is blended with a ridge model; the blend weight is selected by held-out-neuron validation, then both models are refit on all training neurons. Bin predictions are expanded back to 100 Hz, preserving trailing NaNs.", "code_lines": 166, "line_limit_compliant": true, "line_limit_exclusive": 180}

